        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-76939",
        ":question/problem": "![](images/92/9236e136f26433023d806181fcfbef9c05d4976f75e14f74840ae7f48a35da99.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $r=3q$\n\nII. $s=2t$\n\nIII. $p=-s$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $r$ and $q$ have the opposite directions. So, $r\\ne 3q.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, vectors $s$ and $t$ are parallel and have the same directions. Also, the magnitude of $s$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $t.$ So, $s=2t.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $p$ and $s$ are parallel and have the opposite directions. Also, their magnitudes are the same. So, $p=-s.$\n\nTherefore, statements II and III are true, and statement I is false."
      },
